    "wikipedia_summary": "<b><i>Nepenthes</i> × <i>ventrata</i></b> (/nɪˈpɛnθiːz vɛnˈtrɑːtə/) is a natural hybrid involving <i>N. graciliflora </i> and <i>N. ventricosa</i>. Like its two parent species, it is endemic to the Philippines. The name was originally published in the <i>Carnivorous Plant Newsletter</i> in 1979. <i>Nepenthes</i> × <i>ventrata</i> is one of the most common tissue cultured <i>Nepenthes</i> plants, although it is often mislabelled as <i>Nepenthes alata</i>. It is relatively easy to grow indoors and is usually the first tropical pitcher plant seen...",
